<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian official reserves fall in January.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian official reserves fall in January.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's holdings of gold and foreign exchange assets fell to US$16.758 billion in January from US$17.402 billion in December, compared with US$14.428 billion in January 1996, the Reserve Bank of Australia said.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, reserves rose by A$144 million to A$21.992 billion in January from A$21.848 billion in December, compared with A$19.375 billion a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Individual reserve assets in Australian dollars were -</p>
<p>			     Jan 1997	  Dec 1996	 Jan 1996</p>
<p>    Gold		3.58 billion    3.66 billion   4.30 billion</p>
<p>    SDRs		  46 million	46 million     72 million</p>
<p>IMF Reserve position</p>
<p>			   611 million     604 million    659 million</p>
<p>Foreign Exchange</p>
<p>			 17.75 billion   17.54 billion  14.34 billion</p>
<p>    TOTAL:	   21.99 billion   21.85 billion  19.38 billion</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
